ftdi-spi-linux (1.5) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  * Park the GPIO IRQ poll thread while no GPIO line events are requested,
    so an interface with no IRQ consumers stops polling USB at 1 kHz and
    stays out of the load average.
  * Allocate the USB transfer buffers from ZONE_DMA. The BCM2711 dwc2
    controller only reaches the low 1 GiB of RAM, so buffers outside that
    window were bounced through SWIOTLB on every transfer.
  * Unregister the SPI platform device when probe fails after it has been
    added, instead of only dropping a reference. A leaked device kept the
    name registered and made every later probe fail with -EEXIST until the
    machine was rebooted.

 -- David Smith <mmb-davidsmith@users.noreply.github.com>  Thu, 17 Sep 2026 16:07:10 +0000

